Ma", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "2838", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2013, 7, 21]]}, "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0378-5173(03)00386-7"}, {"key": "ref2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/j.carbpol.2005.03.020"}, {"key": "ref3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00217-005-0111-1"}, {"key": "ref4", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/j.foodhyd.2007.01.007"}, {"key": "ref5", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0260-8774(01)00206-0"}, {"key": "ref6", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1023/A:1022830715565"}], "container-title": ["Journal of Networks"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 2, 5]], "date-time": "2025-02-05T17:02:28Z", "timestamp": 1738774948000}, "score": 33.091457, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://dblp.org/db/journals/jnw/index.html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2013, 7, 21]]}, "references-count": 6, "journal-issue": {"issue": "7", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2013, 7, 21]]}}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.4304/jnw.8.7.1640-1646", "ISSN": ["1796-2056"], "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "1796-2056"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2013, 7, 21]]}}, {"institution": [{"id": [{"id": "https://ror.org/028rypz17", "id-type": "ROR", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "name": "Paris 11"}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 30]], "date-time": "2026-07-30T11:21:17Z", "timestamp": 1785410477471, "version": "3.56.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Agence Bibliographique de l'Enseignement Sup\u00e9rieur", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Techniques d'optimisation pour des donn\u00e9es semi-structur\u00e9es du web s\u00e9mantique</jats:title>\n                <jats:p xml:lang=\"fr\">RDF et SPARQL se sont impos\u00e9s comme mod\u00e8le de donn\u00e9es et langage de requ\u00eates standard pour d\u00e9crire et interroger les donn\u00e9es sur la Toile. D\u2019importantes quantit\u00e9s de donn\u00e9es RDF sont d\u00e9sormais disponibles, sous forme de jeux de donn\u00e9es ou de m\u00e9ta-donn\u00e9es pour des documents semi-structur\u00e9s, en particulier XML. La coexistence et l\u2019interd\u00e9pendance grandissantes entre RDF et XML rendent de plus en plus pressant le besoin de repr\u00e9senter et interroger ces donn\u00e9es conjointement. Bien que de nombreux travaux couvrent la production et la publication, manuelles ou automatiques, d\u2019annotations pour donn\u00e9es semi-structur\u00e9es, peu de recherches ont \u00e9t\u00e9 consacr\u00e9es \u00e0 l\u2019exploitation de telles donn\u00e9es. Cette th\u00e8se pose les bases de la gestion de donn\u00e9es hybrides XML-RDF. Nous pr\u00e9sentons XR, un mod\u00e8le de donn\u00e9es accommodant l\u2019aspect structurel d\u2019XML et la s\u00e9mantique de RDF. Le mod\u00e8le est suffisamment g\u00e9n\u00e9ral pour repr\u00e9senter des donn\u00e9es ind\u00e9pendantes ou interconnect\u00e9es, pour lesquelles chaque n\u0153ud XML est potentiellement une ressource RDF. Nous introduisons le langage XRQ, qui combine les principales caract\u00e9ristiques des langages XQuery et SPARQL. Le langage permet d\u2019interroger la structure des documents ainsi que la s\u00e9mantique de leurs annotations, mais aussi de produire des donn\u00e9es semi-structur\u00e9es annot\u00e9es. Nous introduisons le probl\u00e8me de composition de requ\u00eates dans le langage XRQ et \u00e9tudions de mani\u00e8re exhaustive les techniques d\u2019\u00e9valuation de requ\u00eates possibles. Nous avons d\u00e9velopp\u00e9 la plateforme XRP, implantant les algorithmes d\u2019\u00e9valuation de requ\u00eates dont nous comparons les performances exp\u00e9rimentalement. Nous pr\u00e9sentons une application reposant sur cette plateforme pour l\u2019annotation automatique et manuelle de pages trouv\u00e9es sur la Toile. Enfin, nous pr\u00e9sentons une technique pour l\u2019inf\u00e9rence RDFS dans les syst\u00e8mes de gestion de donn\u00e9es RDF (et par extension XR).</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.70675/32401857z6f92z43d1z9cefz050a5da1b1df", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 31]], "date-time": "2026-03-31T04:18:41Z", "timestamp": 1774930721000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2013, 9, 27]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Database techniques for semantics-rich semi-structured Web data"], "prefix": "10.70675", "author": [{"given": "Julien", "family": "Leblay", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"id": [{"id": "https://ror.org/028rypz17", "id-type": "ROR", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "name": "Paris 11"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "51494", "contributor": [{"sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [null]}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 31]], "date-time": "2026-03-31T04:18:44Z", "timestamp": 1774930724000}, "score": 33.083576, "degree": ["Doctorat \u00e8s Informatique (Bases de donn\u00e9es)", "PhD"], "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://theses.fr/2013PA112193"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "alternative-id": ["2013PA112193"], "URL": "https://doi.org/10.70675/32401857z6f92z43d1z9cefz050a5da1b1df"}, {"institution": [{"name": "Nanyang Technological University"}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 4, 2]], "date-time": "2022-04-02T03:41:55Z", "timestamp": 1648870915811}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Nanyang Technological University", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.32657/10356/35745", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 2]], "date-time": "2019-10-02T11:38:27Z", "timestamp": 1570016307000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2007]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Mining evolution of structure of semi-structured web data"], "prefix": "10.32657", "author": [{"giv